Catalog data sources
====================

The embedded catalog (`catalog.bin`, format RPCAT001) is packed by
`crates/rp-catalog/scripts/pack_catalog.py` from the CSV files in this
directory plus a fetched star layer. Per-source provenance:

OpenNGC (messier.csv, ngc.csv, ic.csv, aliases.csv)
---------------------------------------------------

Derived from the OpenNGC catalogue at

    https://github.com/mattiaverga/OpenNGC

by `scripts/openngc_to_catalog.py` (canonical name, object type, ICRS
RA/Dec, V or B magnitude, major-axis size; the "Common names" column
populated `aliases.csv`).

OpenNGC is published under **Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 International (CC-BY-SA-4.0)** —
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
Attribution: openNGC by Mattia Verga, 2018-present.

SIMBAD (sh2, barnard, ldn, lbn, rcw, gum, ced, abell, arp, hcg,
collinder, melotte, stock, trumpler .csv; aliases_simbad.csv)
----------------------------------------------------------------

Positions, object types, magnitudes, sizes, and NAME cross-identifiers
fetched from the SIMBAD database, CDS, Strasbourg, via TAP by
`scripts/fetch_dso_catalogs.py`. Sharpless positions deliberately come
from SIMBAD's curated data rather than the original 1959 list (VizieR
VII/20), whose coordinates are unreliable for some entries.

    This work made use of the SIMBAD database, operated at CDS,
    Strasbourg, France (Wenger et al. 2000, A&AS 143, 9).

CDS data are reusable with attribution (https://cds.unistra.fr/).
SIMBAD's identifier coverage of the Collinder, Melotte, and Gum lists
is partial; the missing numbers are mostly objects whose primary
designation is NGC/IC, which already have rows of their own.

VizieR VII/21 (vdb.csv)
-----------------------

van den Bergh reflection nebulae (van den Bergh 1966, AJ 71, 990),
VizieR catalogue VII/21, fetched by `scripts/fetch_dso_catalogs.py`
using the VizieR-computed J2000 positions. Same CDS attribution terms
as above.

VizieR IV/25 + I/259 (star layer inside catalog.bin only)
---------------------------------------------------------

The star layer is every HD/HDE/HDEC designation in the Tycho-2/HD
cross-index (Fabricius et al. 2002, A&A 386, 709; VizieR IV/25) with
the VizieR-computed J2000 (Tycho-2-derived) positions — not the
original epoch-1900 HD positions — and Johnson V magnitudes
approximated from Tycho-2 (Høg et al. 2000, A&A 355, L27; VizieR
I/259) as V ≈ VT − 0.090·(BT − VT). Fetched by
`scripts/fetch_star_layer.py` into an uncommitted intermediate; only
the packed rows are committed. Same CDS attribution terms as above.

IAU Catalog of Star Names (named_stars.csv)
-------------------------------------------

Proper star names from the IAU Working Group on Star Names (WGSN),
converted by `scripts/fetch_iau_csn.py` from

    https://www.pas.rochester.edu/~emamajek/WGSN/IAU-CSN.txt

IAU products are released under **Creative Commons Attribution**
(https://www.iau.org/public/themes/naming_stars/).

Curated additions (aliases_curated.csv)
---------------------------------------

Hand-maintained common names absent from both OpenNGC and SIMBAD
(e.g. "Tulip Nebula" → Sh2-101). Original to this repository.

